  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Health System Strengthing Approach to Tackling Occupational Health Challenges by Migrant Workers-Integrating Occupational An Migrant Health into National Health System (no.3)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the project &#x2018;Tackling occupational health challenges among Mozambican miners and migrant workers&#x2019;, IOM will support the Government of Mozambique to transition the IOM managed Occupational Health interventions managed by IOM into the national health system.   Through a phased approach, IOM will provide technical and coordination support to the Ministry of Health (MISAU), to ensure (1) continuity of service provision at the three occupational health centres, (2) that strengthened national capacity in occupational health diagnosis are integrated into the national health system, (3) data collection, storage, processing and sharing mechanisms are streamlined and integrated into the national reporting systems to improve the documentation and reporting on the burden of occupational illnesses, and (4), support coordination of multisectoral cross-border partnerships and the institutionalization of referral mechanisms. This initiative will support MISAU to further strengthen national capacity to prevent and detect occupational illnesses in migrant worker populations across the Southern provinces of Mozambique, and generate quality data to support the Government of Mozambique and Mozambican miners to document occupational health conditions, ultimately informing policy and proving access to compensation mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
